Subject: [PATCH] local: wifi: ath12k: send the selected scan priority to firmware

ath12k_wmi_send_scan_start_cmd() selects MEDIUM priority while 11d scan
offload is being prepared and LOW otherwise, but only updates the host
argument. It never copies that value into the WMI command. The command
buffer is zeroed, so firmware receives VERY_LOW for every normal scan.

The 11d offload implementation raises the first host scan's priority to
avoid preemption by the firmware's MEDIUM-priority country discovery.
Restore the missing little-endian assignment so firmware receives the
priority the driver selected.

On the Yoga Slim 7x/WCN7850, the unpatched journal shows about 16.1 seconds
between supplicant availability and connection activation on cold boot,
two hibernate restores and two s2idle resumes. Country discovery completes
about 7.2 seconds into that interval. Authentication and DHCP are quick.
The missing assignment is a source-proven defect; whether it accounts for
that delay still needs a patched hardware comparison.

Log successful submission of the initial MEDIUM-priority scan so the test
can identify the corrected path with CONFIG_ATH12K_DEBUG disabled. This
marker proves command submission, not firmware scheduling or scan success.

Link: https://lists.infradead.org/pipermail/ath12k/2025-March/006346.html
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wmi.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wmi.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wmi.c
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wmi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wmi.c
@@ -2684,6 +2684,7 @@ int ath12k_wmi_send_scan_start_cmd(struct ath12k *ar,
 		arg->scan_priority = WMI_SCAN_PRIORITY_MEDIUM;
 	else
 		arg->scan_priority = WMI_SCAN_PRIORITY_LOW;
+	cmd->scan_priority = cpu_to_le32(arg->scan_priority);
 	cmd->notify_scan_events = cpu_to_le32(arg->notify_scan_events);
 
 	ath12k_wmi_copy_scan_event_cntrl_flags(cmd, arg);
@@ -2800,6 +2801,10 @@ int ath12k_wmi_send_scan_start_cmd(struct ath12k *ar,
 		ath12k_warn(ar->ab, "failed to send WMI_START_SCAN_CMDID\n");
 		dev_kfree_skb(skb);
 	}
+	if (!ret && ar->state_11d == ATH12K_11D_PREPARING)
+		ath12k_info(ar->ab,
+			    "scan: initial scan priority %u submitted to firmware\n",
+			    arg->scan_priority);
 
 	return ret;
 }
